bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (aarch64 JIT, base e2479b4127a0a3a9 and the typed f64? reader fix; interpreter 0.1): val d: {text: f64} = {"k": 0.1}; print d["k"] prints 0.09999999999999998, and val g: f64? = d.get("k") then g ?? 9.0 / if val / unwrap / match all read 0.09999999999999998. MIR stores the literal through rt_dict_set with the raw f64 value and reads it with rt_index_get / rt_dict_get + UnboxFloat, so the raw bits are decoded as a tagged float. Found while probing Option producers for seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27; not an Option representation defect."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, P3, open, "Seed JIT: {text: f64} literal value read back through d[k] / d.get(k) loses the low 3 mantissa bits", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/mir/lower/lowering_expr_collection.rs, 0, NONE, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true
